            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for forward, then the Spanish for the detour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: el indicador",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el indicador — \"the signpost, the sign; the gauge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sigue los indicadores hacia el centro. Follow the signs for the centre."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In a car, el indicador also shows the fuel or the speed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "indicador is built on indicar \"to point out\", a learned borrowing from Latin indicāre (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
